517	// --- landing THIS cycle's PR when the arm could not (#649) --------------------
518	// The disposal above is correct and a full day late. On a member whose
519	// pull_request run is gated, EVERY cycle's arm fails, so every converge waits for
520	// the next cycle to land it — a standing ~24h offset between canon and that
521	// member's main, which reads as a mount that is permanently stale.
522	//
523	// The evidence that settles it does not take a day to arrive: the dispatched run
524	// this cycle just started finishes in seconds. So we wait for it, once, and merge
525	// on exactly the reasoning disposal uses. Same decision, made now.
526	//
527	// Bounded and cheap because it only runs where the arm ALREADY failed: a healthy
528	// member arms and returns without waiting at all. The bound is well inside
529	// `prework_timeout` (900s), and hitting it costs nothing — the PR is
530	// simply left for the next cycle, exactly as before this existed.
531	export const LAND_TIMEOUT_MS = 180_000;
532	export const LAND_POLL_MS = 5_000;
533	
534	// What one poll of the head sha's runs says to do: `merge`, `poll` again, or
535	// `give-up` and leave the PR standing.
536	//
537	// It NEVER closes. Disposal may close a PR because that PR is last cycle's and
538	// this cycle is about to re-cut it; here the PR IS this cycle's delivery, and
539	// closing it would throw away the converge that just ran. A red member therefore
540	// leaves its PR open for the next cycle to dispose of properly — the behaviour
541	// that existed before this, reached deliberately rather than by omission.
542	// `expected` is how many verification runs THIS worker dispatched on the head
543	// seconds ago. Fewer visible runs than that is the API still registering them —
544	// a POLL, never a verdict. Without it, the first read 0.3s after the dispatch
545	// found an empty list and judged "nothing will ever verify this", stranding
546	// seven members' green PRs in one forced fleet pass (2026-08-07).
547	export function landAttempt({ delivery, runs, expected = 0, elapsedMs = 0, timeoutMs = LAND_TIMEOUT_MS }) {
548	  if ((runs ?? []).length < expected) return elapsedMs >= timeoutMs ? 'give-up' : 'poll';
549	  const disposition = pullDisposition({ delivery, runs });
550	  if (disposition === 'merge') return 'merge';
551	  if (disposition === 'wait') return elapsedMs >= timeoutMs ? 'give-up' : 'poll';
552	  return 'give-up';
553	}
