574	// Deliver the converge as one commit on a FRESH per-cycle maintenance branch,
575	// native git: dispose of the family's open PR first (merge it if last cycle's
576	// content is verified, otherwise close it), then cut a new dated branch + PR and
577	// arm auto-merge when the member asked for it.
578	//
579	// Nothing is reused. A maintenance PR is one cycle's deterministic converge, and
580	// a cycle that did not land has nothing to hand the next one — inheriting it is
