635	
636	  // ARM GitHub's native auto-merge (not an immediate merge): the PR lands
637	  // automatically once this repo's required checks pass, and the run never blocks
638	  // on CI. Auto-merge is a GraphQL-only mutation.
639	  //
640	  // Every cycle opens its own PR and arms it, so the arm is never stale — and it
641	  // is no longer the only thing standing between a converge and `main`: the arm
642	  // failing (auto-merge off, or a gated pull_request run) now costs one cycle,
643	  // not forever, because the next cycle merges this PR on its concluded runs
644	  // (pullDisposition) or closes it and re-cuts. Idempotent either way.
645	  // Start the PR's checks FIRST — the GITHUB_TOKEN push/open above emitted no
